Verdict: PASS. It's written to session_plan/eval_task_2.md.

• The fix: the new module src/prompt/stream_aborted_text.rs keeps the text deltas of the message currently streaming. It fills them in only when an assistant message is both aborted and empty, in that message's messageEnd and in agentEnd. It uses the existing text field, so there's no new event type. Every other event goes out unchanged.
• Unit tests: five tests cover the three required cases (aborted and empty gets filled; a normal end and an aborted message that already has text are unchanged). They also cover a retry dropping the first attempt's text and an abort with nothing streamed.
• Binary tests: I ran the three signal tests in tests/output_failed_run.rs (SIGTERM, SIGHUP, SIGINT) against the built binary and all passed. Each one now checks that the agentEnd text equals the streamed partial reply.
• Commit body: it covers what the task asked for:
  • the before-row from a local stub;
  • the yoagent finding (0.27.9 drops the streamed text; upstream ask #1237);
  • the neutered-then-restored check;
  • the 2-second no-agentEnd case, not probed and carried in #1238.
• Size: src/prompt.rs grew by 3 lines (3993 → 3996), and its entry in tests/module_size.rs is updated with a reason.
• Docs: the stream-json paragraph in docs/src/usage/piped-mode.md now says what the closing event carries.

Nothing in the diff is defined without being used. The only stray change is a line appended to .yoyo/risk_validations.jsonl, which looks harmless.
